<figure id="S4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Results of Corrective relearning. In this setting, we fine-tune the unlearned model in Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.2 Diverse Experimental Scenarios for OFFSIDE ‣ 4 Experiment ‣ OFFSIDE: Benchmarking Unlearning Misinformation in Multimodal Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> on <math id="S4.T4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\textbf{relearn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">relearn</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\textbf{relearn}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The best results of five baselines are highlighted in <span id="S4.T4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#CCFFFF;">blue</span>. The results of vanilla model directly skip the unlearning stage and relearn the facts.</figcaption>
<div id="S4.T4.4" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:466.3pt;height:118.1pt;vertical-align:-57.6pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-175.9pt,44.5pt) scale(0.6,0.6) ;">
